2\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.6.2\n\n### Issue description\n\nCurrently, signals inside XRController3D such as these below will cause the SHADOWED_VARIABLE_BASE_CLASS warning to show up as \"The local function parameter \"name\" is shadowing an already-declared property in the base class \"Node\".\" whenever we connect these signals to a script:\n\n```button_pressed(name: String)```\n```button_released(name: String)```\n```input_float_changed(name: String, value: float)```\n```input_vector2_changed(name: String, value: Vector2)```\n\nWhile I can change the parameter name after connecting it to a script to avoid the warnings, it's a slight inconvenience.\n\n<img width=\"1721\" height=\"560\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63a9a9a3-cda6-48ec-aede-6bc5886a7e15\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create an XRController3D node.\n2. Add a script to a node.\n3. Connect ```button_pressed(name: String)```, ```button_released(name: String)```, ```input_float_changed(name: String, value: float)```, and/or ```input_vector2_changed(name: String, value: Vector2)``` to the script.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_even